# ...except the web engine's own build output. `packages/sdk/wasm` is committed
# so that cloning the repository and running `npm install` is enough to play and
# build games: no Rust toolchain, no wasm-pack, no C++ linker. Rebuild it with
# `npm run build:wasm` after changing anything under `crates/`, and commit the
# result -- CI fails if the checked-in bindings drift from the Rust source.
*.wasm

# `package-lock.json` is the lockfile this repository validates: CI installs
# with `npm ci`, so it cannot silently rot. A `bun.lock` used to live here too
# and did rot -- it still pinned the web engine to `crates/platform-web/pkg`
# long after that output moved, so `bun install` failed on a fresh clone even
# though npm limped along. Bun resolves fine from `package.json` alone; let it
# write its own lockfile locally rather than shipping a second, unchecked one.
bun.lock
bun.lockb

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.history/

